Configure the Converters that Transport Parts to and from ProcessingB
Insert and configure the Converters that convey the parts to and from the station ProcessingB.
Proceed as follows:
• As we want to convey the parts laterally to the station ProcessingB depending on their name, open
ConverterToB and select the Strategy > MU Name.
• Then, click Open List and enter the names of the parts which we want to move to the station
ProcessingB into the list. We want the parts named B1, B2, and B3 to be conveyed laterally to the
left, enter their names and select side 3 in the attribute list. As you remember, the numbers designate
the side of the Converter at which the part exits.
Configure the Converters that Transport Parts to and from ProcessingB
Plant Simulation Help 10-713
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• As we want to convey the parts arriving from ProcessingB straight on, open ConverterFromB, and select
the Strategy > MU Name.
• Then, click Open List and enter the names of the parts which you want to move on into the list. We
want the parts named B1, B2, and B3 to be conveyed straight on, so enter their names and select the
side 0 in the attribute list.
• Start the simulation and watch how the Converters convert the parts laterally to the left and straight on
depending on their name. To better recognize that they do this correctly, we drew an icon with an arrow
pointing in the direction of motion.
You will notice that the right hand side of the part points downwards after it has moved from
ConverterToB into the processing station. This is because moving the part laterally to the left rotates
it 90 degrees clockwise.
Once the part moves from the processing station to ConverterFromB, it is rotated another 90 degrees
clockwise, thus moving backward toward the Drain, which removes it from the installation.
