Conveying Parts According to a Strategy Control
Convey Parts According to a Strategy Control
In this sample model the Source produces 10 parts each of three different types. It moves the parts to a
Converter, which conveys them laterally to the left, laterally to the right, or straight through according to
their names. We programmed where exactly each type goes in a Strategy Control.
Conveying Parts According to a Strategy Control
10-714 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

In our examples we will:
• Configure the Source that Produces the Parts [Converter, laterally]
• Configure the Converter that Conveys the Parts
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Back to Convey Parts Laterally with the Converter
Configure the Source that Produces the Parts [Converter]
Insert and configure the Source which produces the parts.
Proceed as follows:
• Select when and how many parts of a certain type are to be produced.
Select a Delivery Table in our example, as shown in the screenshot below.
Configure the Source that Produces the Parts [Converter]
Plant Simulation Help 10-715
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Then select the name of the delivery table, which we inserted before, namely the DataTable. Selecting it
automatically applied the correct format.
Enter the required information, as shown the screenshot below.
The Source then produces the parts with the settings above and the Converter conveys them to the
connected objects.
Back to Convey Parts According to a Strategy Control
Configure the Converter that Conveys the Parts
Insert and configure the Converter that conveys the parts.
Proceed as follows:
• As we want to convey the parts—depending on their type—laterally or straight on to the stations
connected to the Converter, select the Strategy > Method.
Configure the Converter that Conveys the Parts
10-716 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To create the control, right-click into the text box Strategy Method and select Create Control. Plant
Simulation then enters self.OnStrategy and opens the method.
Then, type in the following source code. It conveys the parts named A laterally to the left, i.e., to exit 3
of the Converter, the parts named B laterally to the right, i.e., to exit 1, and the parts named C straight
on, i.e., to exit 0 of the Converter.
param entranceNo: integer
if @.name = "C" 
   ?.ExitForMU := 0 /* number of the exit of the converter*/
elseif @.name = "A" 
  if entranceNo = 2 
       ?.ExitForMU := 3
   else
       ?.ExitForMU := 0
   end
else
   if entranceNo = 2
       ?.ExitForMU := 1
   else
       ?.ExitForMU := 0
   end
end
• Start the simulation and watch how the Converter first moves the 10 parts named A laterally to the left,
the 10 parts named B laterally to the right, and the 10 parts named C straight on.
Back to Convey Parts According to a Strategy Control
